H2: Known Faults ƒ?" Jeep Compass
P: These faults are for the Compass sold in the UK from 2017.
H3: Engines and Jeep Brand Reliability
P: MONITOR ¶ú 2017 on ¶ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says the engines are familiar from other Fiat models and there have been many reported problems. It also says Jeep as a brand finished in 29th place out of 32 manufacturers.
H3: Diesel Particulate Filter (DPF)
P: MONITOR ¶ú Diesel ¶ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says the diesel particulate filters are prone to clogging. It adds that some cars had problems with the diesel engines, often related to this issue, and overly high oil levels after fuel contamination.
H3: Not Starting
P: MONITOR ¶ú 2017-2021 ¶ú Get a quote
P: The RACƒ?Ts review of the 2017-2021 Compass mentions a number of reports of the vehicle not starting, which appears to be down to a malfunctioning battery and various software codes.
H3: Water Leaking Into the Cabin
P: MONITOR ¶ú 2017-2021 ¶ú Get a quote
P: The RAC says it has heard of water leaking into the cabin of the 2017-2021 car.
H3: Automatic Gearbox
P: MONITOR ¶ú 2017-2021 ¶ú Get a quote
P: The RAC reports overheating CVT auto transmissions and autos that make strange whining noises. Auto Express, road testing the 2017 car with the 2.0-litre diesel automatic, said the Compass was also not helped by the slow nine-speed automatic gearbox.
H3: Uconnect Infotainment
P: MINOR ¶ú 2017 on ¶ú Get a quote
P: Auto Express says the Uconnect infotainment system is great to use, but can just switch off. Try it on a test drive.
H3: Diesel Engine Rattle
P: MINOR ¶ú 2017 2.0 diesel ¶ú Get a quote
P: Auto Expressƒ?Ts road test of the 2017 car with the 2.0-litre diesel automatic mentions a very unpleasant diesel rattle.
H3: Plug-in Hybrid Battery Warranty
P: CHECK ¶ú Plug-in hybrid ¶ú Check the warranty
P: Jeep UKƒ?Ts plug-in hybrid page covers the Compass. It says these cars come with an 8-year and 100,000 miles battery standard warranty and a standard vehicle warranty for up to 3 years. Ask the seller what is left on the car you are looking at.
H3: DVSA Safety Recalls
P: DVSAƒ?Ts recall data lists several Compass recalls, including these.
LI: On certain vehicles the under-seat intermediate connection or the rear connection to the Integrated Dual Charging Module (IDCM) may not be tightened to the proper torque which may cause overheating of the terminal with risk of thermal incident to surrounding parts.
LI: On affected vehicles The PBU (pressure valve) membrane in the high voltage battery pack may not be sealed due to incomplete ultrasonic welding.
LI: The body control module software may allow engine stop start behaviour that was not part of the emissions certification.
LI: The rear seat back release latch housing may become damaged and unlatched.
P: Enter the registration in our recall check to see whether a car has a recall that is still open.
