H2: Known Faults ƒ?" Jeep Grand Cherokee
H3: Patchy Reliability, 2005-2011
P: MONITOR ¶ú 2005-2011 cars ¶ú Get a quote
P: Auto Express reviews the Mk3 Grand Cherokee, built from 2005 to 2011, and says reliability can be patchy. Its advice is to check the car and its history very carefully before committing to a purchase.
H3: Electrics on the 2005-2011 Cars
P: MONITOR ¶ú 2005-2011 cars ¶ú Get a quote
P: Carbuyerƒ?Ts owner page for the 2005-2011 Grand Cherokee has a common problems panel. It lists electrics with four cases, gearbox and clutch with two cases and the engine with one case.
H3: Corrosion, Door Seals and Injection Return Rail
P: CHECK ¶ú One ownerƒ?Ts report ¶ú Get a quote
P: One Parkers owner of a 2005-2010 3.0 CRD Limited wrote of several things: underbody corrosion that Jeep deemed commercially acceptable, door seals rubbing the paintwork, and engine and transmission faults. The owner also reported one injection return rail left unsecured, which caused massive fuel loss into the engine bay and underbody.
H3: Sunroof and Flat Battery
P: CHECK ¶ú One ownerƒ?Ts report ¶ú Get a quote
P: A Parkers owner of a 2005-2010 3.0 CRD Overland wrote that the sunroof drained the battery within two years but was fixed with a software upgrade.
H3: Low-Range Selection and Driveline
P: CHECK ¶ú Ownersƒ?T reports ¶ú Get a quote
P: A Parkers owner of a 2005-2010 3.0 CRD Overland Tech reported only the low range selection, which they said was about to be sorted. A Parkers owner of a 2005-2010 3.0 CRD Overland wrote that the driveline and associated electronics were an absolute nightmare.
H3: Boot Lock and Sat Nav
P: CHECK ¶ú One ownerƒ?Ts report ¶ú Get a quote
P: A Carbuyer owner of a 2011 car, listed on the 2005-2011 owner page, wrote of a couple of faults: the boot lock had failed and the sat nav plays up. Both were being attended to, the owner said, and they wanted to see the outcome after the dealer had fixed them.
H3: Transmission Snatch, 2011-2020
P: MONITOR ¶ú 2011-2020 cars ¶ú Get a quote
P: A Parkers owner of a 2011-2020 3.0 CRD Overland Summit wrote that, due to the torque band range, too many revs result in transmission snatch and a sudden speed pick-up. A Parkers owner of an Overland 3.0 MultiJet II wrote that it is nigh on impossible to drive smoothly at low revs, because the torque band does not produce wheel motion, then the transmission bites and they end up on the throttle and brake continuously.
H3: Electrics on the 2011-2021 Cars
P: MONITOR ¶ú 2011-2021 cars ¶ú Get a quote
P: Carbuyerƒ?Ts owner page for the 2011-2021 Grand Cherokee has its own common problems panel. Electrics appear in several of its entries, alongside gearbox and clutch, engine and other.
H3: Repeated Breakdowns and Unreliability, Ownersƒ?T Reports
P: CHECK ¶ú Ownersƒ?T reports ¶ú Get a quote
P: A Carbuyer owner of a 2012 car wrote that it had returned to various dealers repeatedly, mostly on a tow truck. A Parkers owner of a 2011-2020 3.0 CRD Limited wrote that the whole experience is ruined as it is just shockingly unreliable.
H3: Beeping for No Reason
P: MINOR ¶ú One ownerƒ?Ts report ¶ú Get a quote
P: A Parkers owner of a 2011-2020 3.0 CRD Summit wrote that they had no issues whatsoever, apart from every now and again the car beeps for no reason, as if it senses something and needs to warn the driver of something.
P: For the engines, trims and years behind each version, see our Jeep Grand Cherokee parts guide . To find out whether a DVSA safety recall is open on a car, put its registration into our recall check .
