P: Initial MOT tests in Great Britain, 2025, from DVSA's anonymised MOT data; fail rate as DVSA calculates it (fails plus faults fixed during the test). Results cover every car recorded under the model name, so the older age bands can include earlier generations of it. Contains public sector information licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0. MOT pass rates for every model and how they're worked out .
H2: More for the Jeep Wrangler
LI: All Jeep Wrangler guides
LI: Jeep Wrangler parts prices
H2: Frequently asked questions
P: Auto Express says most owners call their Jeeps very reliable and superb off road, and Parkers says Wranglers don&#39;t seem to be too affected by major issues. RAC Drive&#39;s JK review lists individual faults, including a stalling petrol car, a leaking fuel tank and a broken seat belt.
P: TJ (1996 to 2006): Autocar lists the 2.5-litre petrol, water pump and manifold faults on the 4.0-litre, a seizing transfer box, a cracking rear differential washer and chassis rot on parallel imports. JK (2007 to 2018): oil use on the 3.8-litre V6, leaks, and worn dampers and ball joints. JL (2018 onwards): short battery life, loose fuses and damaged windscreens.
P: RAC Drive says to feel how the gearbox shifts, watch for unstable handling, jerks or vibrations, and listen for unexpected idling, stuttering and loud ticking. Auto Express adds checking for tired dampers, worn ball joints, torn driveshaft gaiters and water in the car.
P: Enter the registration in our [recall check](/car-recall-check) to see whether a DVSA safety recall is open on a particular car, because recalls depend on the exact vehicle.
