H2: Known Faults ƒ?" Jeep Avenger
P: The points below come from What Car?, Carbuyer and DVSA recall data, and each says where it comes from.
H3: Jeep Reliability Record
P: MONITOR ¶ú Any miles ¶ú N/A
P: What Car? says Jeepƒ?Ts poor reliability record gives reason for concern as a used buy, and that Jeep has finished near the bottom of its brand rankings in recent years. Carbuyer says that like all Jeeps, the Avenger is built tough and should be reliable.
H3: Software Issues
P: CHECK ¶ú One long-term Avenger Electric ¶ú N/A
P: What Car? ran an Avenger Electric as a long-term car and says it encountered a few software issues. The first problem was with the driverƒ?Ts display and infotainment screen, which went blank on start-up. It also says that on one occasion the car refused to start and engage gear. This is the experience of one car, not a survey result. Its advice is to ensure all scheduled software updates have been carried out, so ask the seller for proof.
H3: Stop-Start
P: MINOR ¶ú Carbuyerƒ?Ts test car ¶ú N/A
P: Carbuyer says the stop-start in its test car was a bit unpredictable, which may lead to a lot of owners simply turning it off. That is one test car. DVSA also lists a stop-start recall, covered below.
H3: DVSA Safety Recalls
P: DVSAƒ?Ts recall data lists several Avenger recalls, including these.
LI: On some vehicles the Electronics Stability Control (ESC) warning light and the relative warning message may appear on the Instrument Panel Cluster (IPC) and the ESC may deactivate.
LI: On affected vehicles due to a production nonconformity there may be contact or a reduced clearance between the fuel Particulate Filter pipe and the pole protection cup of the 48V Belt Starter Generator.
LI: On affected vehicles due to a production nonconformity there is a requirement to inspect the brake pedal bracket connection and if necessary perform a rework to eliminate any potential risk of brake pedal disengagement.
LI: On a number of Jeep Avenger ICE (internal combustion engine) vehicles equipped with start/stop function and manual transmission the Stop&#x26;Start function may not activate correctly.
LI: A number of Jeep Avenger BEV vehicles may not comply with emissions test requirements conducted by the relevant authorities.
